      <uighur>ǰayisang</uighur>
      <cyrillic>зайсан(г)</cyrillic>
      <transcript>ZAISANG</transcript>
      <definition>[Ch. tsai-hsiang] n. An honorary title used mostly among the western Mongols (Oirats) for the head of a clan; equivalent of a taizi, q. v. In Mongolia proper this word is now used for the chief or head of a clan or group of people under a Khutukhtu administration.</definition>
      <page>1027</page>
